RecordTrail sets the processes of a quality system as stations on one record trail, each station dropping the record sheet it leaves on a cord, the trail ending in a stack of sheets.

- On the site: a `table` block (`as: "evidence"`) with `"look": "record-trail"` (renderer `assets/src/blocks/look-record-trail.js`), cmp-quality "Each process, and the record it leaves". Origin: pass 12 concept 240 (`240-p12-cmp-quality-record-sheet.png`: numbered stations on one steel-blue rail, each dropping a named sheet, the last onto a stack). Replaces RecordSheet on that page; RecordSheet stays in the library. Not copied from the concept: the page-title and wordmark stand-ins, sheets hanging at random heights.
- Markup: `<div class="aq-record-trail">` > `p.__key` (aria-hidden: node, text and sheet named with the block's three column names) + `__run` > (Fold) `ol.__list` > `li.__st` (`is-row-end`, `is-last`; `--rt-rest` when the last row is short) > `i.__rail`, `i.__node`, `i.__turn` (`i.__tr`, `i.__tl`) or `i.__end` (aria-hidden line work), `__hang` (`h3.__name` with `__n`, `p.__ctl` with an `__k` screen-reader label), `__sheet` (`p.__sk` > `__k`, `ul` > `li` > text + `svg.__g` with `path.__ink`, `path.__acc`); then `__stack` (aria-hidden: `__count`, `svg.__pile` > `path.__ps`, `path.__pr`).
- Fields: `cols [process, what it controls, record you can inspect]`, `rows` (strings or `{t, link}`), `fold`, `fold_noun` (phones only). Records split at ";". Glyph kinds as RecordSheet (certificate, register, log, minutes, list, request or assessment, CAPA or check, report or NCR, records; else a plain sheet). The stack's caption counts the processes (the rows); it does not count records.
- Layout (desktop): four stations a row (`--rt-gap` 32 px columns, `--rt-row` 64 px between rows, a 32 px right lane `--rt-lane` for the turns); the rail turns down the lane, back along the gutter and down into the next row's first node; after the last station it drops to the stack at the bottom right. Sheets align at the foot of their row. 861 to 1100 px: tighter gaps and 17 px names.
- Tokens: rail, cord and turns 1.5 px `line-strong`; nodes an `ink` ring on `surface`; names 19 px `ink`, text 15 px `ink-muted`; sheets `surface-raised` with a `line-strong` hairline and a folded corner (`surface-sunken`); records 14 px with an `ink-subtle` glyph and a `flow` accent; the stack's top sheet ruled in `flow`. Mono 12 px for numbers, key and count.
- Hover / focus: the station's node fills `flow-tint` with a `flow` ring, its cord turns `flow`, its sheet lifts 3 px with a `flow` edge.
- Phone (860 px container or less): the rail runs down the left (node at 0, content at 32 px); each station stacks number and name, what it controls (15 px) and its sheet; the rail's end curl closes the trail and the stack is not shown on phones. 600 to 860 px: each sheet hangs beside its station (two columns). Fold after `fold` stations (3 on cmp-quality) with the 44 px button. No PhoneKit: every station is already one readable unit and the trail is the figure.
- Motion (`motion.js`): ported from Subframe Motion "Causal cadence" (causal-cadence), MIT: the rail draws node to node (0.3 s, power3.out) and each sheet drops 16 px on its cord, cued from the node's arrival plus 0.12 s; the turns fade in with the row end; the stack takes its sheets last. Desktop plays the whole trail once (under 3.6 s); phones play each station as it scrolls in. Reduced motion: the finished trail.
- Not for: a sequence the reader must follow in time (ProcessSteps, CutoverSchedule) or documents delivered with a system (DocList, IndexSheet).
